  appreciationDetails            String?                 @map("appreciation_details") @db.Text
  policyAgreementAccepted        Boolean                 @default(false) @map("policy_agreement_accepted")
  policyAgreementAcceptedAt      DateTime?               @map("policy_agreement_accepted_at")
  /// The Login Credentials page of onboarding, half-filled and put down.
  ///
  /// Creating a login is one screen's worth of decisions - the username and address, the roles, the
  /// branch, who covers for this person - and it was routinely interrupted. Nothing on that page
  /// belonged anywhere until the account existed, so closing the panel threw all of it away. This is
  /// where it waits: what was chosen, not an account. No `User` row is created, nothing is emailed,
  /// and none of it is in force until **Create User & Send Email** is pressed.
  ///
  /// Cleared the moment that happens - the account is then the truth, and a draft left beside it
